WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.217
Deterministic ordering means the same data should produce the same row sequence every time.

00:00:06.217 --> 00:00:10.222
Suppose two employees have exactly the same salary.

00:00:10.222 --> 00:00:19.382
If row number is ordered only by salary, the database has no business rule that says which tied employee should come

00:00:19.382 --> 00:00:26.402
first. Adding employee I D as a second ordering value gives the query a stable tie-breaker.

00:00:26.402 --> 00:00:28.072
Be careful, though.

00:00:28.072 --> 00:00:36.442
If you add employee I D to a rank calculation, the two salary values may no longer be treated as true peers.

00:00:36.442 --> 00:00:39.532
The ordering rule must match the meaning you want.
